+## deadlock.5 — durable request tracking and dispatch recovery
+
+- Dev deliveries show the task key, assigned branch/worktree, and whether execution stopped before invocation, reached the worker, or returned a result. A returned result is still not a task-specific ACK.
+- Worktree preflight failures distinguish a missing target from a non-Git path or wrong branch and include the expected tuple.
+- Each GitHub watcher request gets its own durable queue row. A stable event key deduplicates poll retries without collapsing distinct requests into one mutable message.
+- Queue priority ages every 60 seconds, so fresh PO/PM work starts promptly while older requests cannot be starved indefinitely by a stream of newer events.
+- A held unrelated Dev task no longer suppresses a different active task's wake. An executing Dev turn or a conflicting active write lease still serializes dispatch.
+- Any failed assigned Dev delivery queues one idempotent PM disposition request. Pre-invocation failures need a corrected route; post-invocation failures require inspection for partial effects. Neither path blindly retries Dev.
+- The retry endpoint enforces the same guard as the UI: failed bound Dev deliveries with a queued PM recovery cannot be replayed; invoked failures require inspection and a fresh task handoff. Recovery notices still reach PM at the automatic handoff-depth limit without spawning another writer.
+- Review polling stores each exact review, inline comment, and requested-reviewer addition/withdrawal. Read failures hold the watcher cursor so review asks are retried rather than silently skipped.
+- PM instructions now require a verified-checkout bootstrap before dispatching to a not-yet-created task worktree.
+
+The live deadlock.4 worker rejected the #1570 assignment before Claude invocation because the new target worktree was not yet present. Its generic error did not identify the missing path, and no PM recovery delivery followed. This patch makes that failure diagnosable and recoverable while keeping the single-writer guard. It also preserves every watcher ask separately until its delivery receives a specific disposition and emits review signals with their source IDs, URLs and text.
+
 ## deadlock.4 — quieter GitHub coordination
 
 - Routine reconciliation updates the board without posting another GitHub comment. Pins, task directives, evidence, blockers and PO decisions still publish.
